/T (MPI \(Message PassingInterface\)isused to run a program using multiple processes. Each process has a unique rank, startingfrom0.MPI_Comm_rank\(\) gives the rank of the current process, while MPI_Comm_size\(\) givesthetotalnumber of processes. When the program is executed with four processes, the ranks are0,1,2and3.)
/E (MPI \(Message PassingInterface\)isused to run a program using multiple processes. Each process has a unique rank, startingfrom0.MPI_Comm_rank\(\) gives the rank of the current process, while MPI_Comm_size\(\) givesthetotalnumber of processes. When the program is executed with four processes, the ranks are0,1,2and3.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
